    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "I am using this config to make the window that mini.clue shows appear under my cursor like an autocompletion window.\r\n\r\n```\r\nwindow = {\r\n  config = {\r\n    relative = 'cursor',\r\n    width = 'auto',\r\n    height = 10,\r\n  },\r\n  delay = 1000,\r\n  scroll_down = '<C-d>',\r\n  scroll_up = '<C-u>',\r\n},\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut it does not work, I still get the window at the bottom right corner of my terminal. Is this supported?",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I am using this config to make the window that mini.clue shows appear under my cursor like an autocompletion window.</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"window = {\n  config = {\n    relative = 'cursor',\n    width = 'auto',\n    height = 10,\n  },\n  delay = 1000,\n  scroll_down = '&lt;C-d&gt;',\n  scroll_up = '&lt;C-u&gt;',\n},\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">window = {\n  config = {\n    relative = 'cursor',\n    width = 'auto',\n    height = 10,\n  },\n  delay = 1000,\n  scroll_down = '&lt;C-d&gt;',\n  scroll_up = '&lt;C-u&gt;',\n},\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">But it does not work, I still get the window at the bottom right corner of my terminal. Is this supported?</p>",
    "bodyText": "I am using this config to make the window that mini.clue shows appear under my cursor like an autocompletion window.\nwindow = {\n  config = {\n    relative = 'cursor',\n    width = 'auto',\n    height = 10,\n  },\n  delay = 1000,\n  scroll_down = '<C-d>',\n  scroll_up = '<C-u>',\n},\n\nBut it does not work, I still get the window at the bottom right corner of my terminal. Is this supported?",
